/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
609 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1242 0 R
/E (Female recall \(60.51%\) was lower than male recall \(66.68%\))
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
610 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1243 0 R
/E (The model correctly identified a smaller proportion of actual high-income females than males.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
611 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (2\) Demographic Audit by Race)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
612 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1244 0 R
/E (Recall varied across recorded race groups, from 57.54% \(Black\) to 70.68% \(Asian-Pac-Islander\).)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
613 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1245 0 R
/E (False Positive Rates \(FPR\) also differed across groups. For example, Black individuals had an FPR of 2.89%, compared with 8.93% for             Asian-Pac-Islander individuals.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
614 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (3\) Overall Interpretation)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
615 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1246 0 R
/E ( Differences in TPR and FPR across sex and race groups suggest potential fairness concerns despite excluding these features from training. However, they do not prove discrimination and estimates for smaller groups may be less reliable due to limited data. Further fairness evaluation is needed before real-world deployment.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
616 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (Why did we conduct this audit?)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
617 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (We excluded `sex` and `race` from model inputs to avoid directly using these sensitive characteristics. However, other features \(e.g. relationships\) may indirectly reflect demographic characteristics so removing them does not guarantee fairness. Thus, we conducted a descriptive demographic audit using True Positive Rate \(TPR\) and False Positive Rate \(FPR\) to examine differences in model performance across demographic groups.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
618 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (The top bar chart shows the demographic audit by sex, while the bottom bar chart shows the demographic audit by race.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
